                StoryPart(10, "A Light Kept Honestly", listOf("The town unveiled a new plaque naming Amara Vale as the harbour wall's designer and recognising the workers who had helped her. Leila donated the original plans to the archive, where anyone could study them.", "Nia repaired the clock with the caretaker and set it to the correct time. The old 8:17 remained in the record book, not as a mystery but as the moment the search began.", "On her last evening in Greyhaven, the lighthouse beam crossed the water and returned safely to shore. Nia understood her grandfather's promise at last: a light was useful only when it helped people see clearly. The secret had been solved, the credit restored, and the town could finally tell its history truthfully.")
